These are a working _non released_ File Lister utes that allows users to
download daily updated lists of your filebase.

"FileLister.c" produces a filelist of _EVERY_ file and file section in your
filebase.  While "FileListerX" uses a config file to exclude those 
sensitive/naughty sections.

To compile the source, you'll need SAS C 6.X.

To use it, you'll need a script that runs nightly, (usually during Fido
poll time), that produces the new file list.

eg:

  delete BBS:Text/BumbleFileList.lha
  dh0:BBS/FileLister/FileLister >ram:files BBS: BBS:Files/
  dh0:c/lha >NIL: a BBS:Text/BumbleFileList.lha ram:files
  delete ram:files

Config file format:

  NO_OF_ENTRIES
  ENTRY1
  ENTRY2
    . 
    .
    .
  ENTRYN


ie:

  5
  90
  91
  92
  93
  94

The users will then need a very simple menu option that allows them to
download the newly generated file, "BBS:Text/BumbleFileList.lha".  Usually from
your logoff screen...


